      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auth): use sanitized profile name for Codex import even without id- prefix",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a profile name collision bug when importing OpenAI Codex auth credentials that lack an explicit `accountId`. Previously, the helper function `resolveOpenAICodexImportProfileName` would only accept the `profileName` if it started with the `id-` prefix; otherwise, it fell back to a hardcoded string parameter (e.g., `codex-import`). If multiple accounts lacking an `accountId` but having different profile names (like email addresses) were imported, they would all fall back to the same name, colliding and overwriting each other.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUpdated `resolveOpenAICodexImportProfileName` in `src/plugin-sdk/provider-openai-chatgpt-auth.ts` to accept the `profileName` regardless of prefix, after sanitizing it to remove illegal characters (such as `@`).\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents credential import collisions when migrating multiple Codex auth profiles that lack explicit account IDs but have distinct profile names.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPassed unit tests on branch `fix/1.5-codex-import-profile-name-collision` in `src/plugin-sdk/provider-openai-chatgpt-auth.test.ts`:\n```\n ✓ |unit-fast| src/plugin-sdk/provider-openai-chatgpt-auth.test.ts (5 tests) 4ms\n```\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nVerified that email-based profile names (e.g. `peter@example.com`) are correctly sanitized to `peter-example.com` instead of falling back to `codex-import`:\n```\nresolveOpenAICodexImportProfileName({ profileName: \"peter@example.com\" }, \"codex-import\")\n// Returns: \"peter-example.com\"\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/1.5-codex-import-profile-name-collision",
